   "he": "מְקַבֵּל עָלָיו מְקוֹם גָּדֵר כּוּ׳. תָּאנָא: חָרִיץ מִבַּחוּץ, וּבֶן חָרִיץ מִבִּפְנִים. וְזֶה וָזֶה אֲחוֹרֵי גָדֵר,",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the buyer «accepts upon himself» to provide out of his own property «the space for the fence» between the two halves of the field and for the larger and smaller ditches. A Sage «taught» in a baraita: The larger «ditch» is dug «on the outside, while the smaller ditch» is dug «on the inside,» closer to the field. Both «this and that» are dug «behind the fence,»"
  }
